A||||5||Formula88||Santa and the FAA||||10||
Z||000000||Formula88||12-13-2001||02:50 PM||||Santa Claus, like all pilots, gets regular visits from the Federal <BR>Aviation Administration, and it was shortly before Christmas when the <BR>FAA examiner arrived.<P>The examiner walked slowly around the sled. He checked the reindeer <BR>harnesses, the landing gear, and Rudolf's nose. He painstakingly <BR>reviewed Santa's weight and balance calculations for the sled's <BR>enormous <BR>payload.<P>Finally, they were ready for the check ride. Santa got in, and the <BR>examiner hopped in carrying, to Santa's surprise, a shotgun.<P>"What's that for?" asked Santa incredulously.<P>The examiner winked and said, "I'm not supposed to tell you this, but <BR>you're gonna lose an engine on takeoff."<BR>||||reg||10
